<title>USA: AT&amp;T,Bell Atlantic,DSC settle.</title>
<headline>AT&amp;T,Bell Atlantic,DSC settle.</headline>
<dateline>DALLAS 1997-02-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>AT&amp;T Corp, Bell Atlantic Corp and DSC Communications Corp said Tuesday they have settled a federal lawsuit involving Caller ID.</p>
<p>Terms of the settlement on the anti-trust lawsuits were not disclosed.</p>
<p>Bell Atlantic and DSC had filed a lawsuit against AT&amp;T, contending that AT&amp;T had &quot;crippled&quot; Caller ID by blocking that information on most long-distance calls, Bell Atlantic spokeswoman Joan Rasmussen said.</p>
<p>A related lawsuit against Lucent Technologies Inc, involving equipment and software, remains unresolved. That case is set for trial on March 4.</p>
</text>
